Kubernetes Outage Scenario: What Would You Do?

Last week, I was testing a cluster where all apps suddenly went down. Pods were in CrashLoopBackOff.
Turns out, the ConfigMap had a misconfigured environment variable — and since all pods depended on it, the failure spread cluster-wide.

This taught me a key lesson:
🔑 ConfigMaps and Secrets are single points of failure if not versioned or validated properly.

✅ Best Practices I picked up:
Keep versioned ConfigMaps/Secrets so you can roll back fast.
Use tools like Kustomize or Helm to manage changes.
Validate configs with CI before applying them.
Consider feature flags to reduce risk of cluster-wide impact.

💡 Takeaway: In Kubernetes, sometimes it’s not the code that breaks production — it’s the config.
